  "description": {
   "en": "Traumatized by the words of her first love, Julius, \nDiana, a baroness, has become a recluse in a country villa.\nShe spends her days making magical tools, which is her forte, and becomes a craftsman who is even called the \"Witch of Römer\".\nOne day, Diana goes to an evening party in the royal capital, where she has a chance encounter with Julius.\nWhile she tries to forget her faint feelings for him, her brother, who is too much of a sissy, develops a “ring to repel men” that repels the insects that come close to Diana, and it discharges into Julius...?"
